      ],
      "extract": "This is a series of 4 lectures on cellular algebras. In the lectures we introduce the theory of cellular algebras which were deﬁned ﬁrst by Graham and Lehrer in 1996 to deal systematically with parameterizing irreducible representations of algebras and related problems. If a ﬁnite-dimensional algebra is given by quiver with relations, the irreducible representations over such an algebra are very easy to describe.",
      "extractCut": true
    }
